                  %a{:href => "#classical_model_structure_on_simplicial_sets"} Classical model structure on simplicial sets
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em classical model structure on simplicial sets
            or
            %em Kan-Quillen model structure
            ,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi sSet
                    %mi Quillen
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet_{Quillen}
            (
            %a{:href => "#Quillen67"}> Quillen 67, II.3
            ) is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+category"} model category
            structure on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
            which represents the standard classical
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
          %p
            Its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalences"} weak equivalences
            are the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+weak+equivalences"} simplicial weak equivalences
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphisms"} isomorphisms
            on
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+homotopy+groups"} simplicial homotopy groups
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrations"} fibrations
            are the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+fibrations"} Kan fibrations
            and its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrations"} cofibrations
            are the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphisms"} monomorphisms
            (degreewise injections).
          %p
            The
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+simplicial+complex"} singular simplicial complex
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization"} geometric realization
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nerve+and+realization"} adjunction
            constitutes a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"} Quillen equivalence
            between
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi sSet
                    %mi Quillen
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet_{Quillen}
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Top
                      %mi Quillen
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top_{Quillen}
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+topological+spaces"} classical model structure on topological spaces
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+hypothesis"} homotopy hypothesis
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "homotopy+hypothesis#ForKanComplexes"} for Kan complexes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category+theory"} (∞,1)-category theory
            this means that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi sSet
                    %mi Quillen
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} sSet_{Quillen}
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Top
                    %mi Quillen
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top_{Quillen}
            both are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presentable+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} presentations
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-category"} (∞,1)-category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9EGrpd"} ∞Grpd
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%88%9E-groupoids"} ∞-groupoids
          %p
            There are also other model structures on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sSet"} sSet
            itself, see at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} model structure on simplicial sets
            for more. This entry here focuses on just the standard classical model structure.
          %h2#background_on_combinatorial_topology Background on combinatorial topology
          %p
            This section reviews basics of the theory of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
            (the modern version of the original “combinatorial topology”) necessary to define, verify and analyse the classical model category structure on simplicial sets,
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#TheClassicalModelStructure"} below
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+homotopy+theory"} simplicial homotopy theory
          %h3#simplicial_sets Simplicial sets
          %p
            The concept of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
            is secretly well familiar already in basic
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+topology"} algebraic topology
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+simplicial+complexes"} singular simplicial complexes
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+homology"} singular homology
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+cohomology"} singular cohomology
          %p
            Conversely, every simplicial set may be
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+realization"} geometrically realized
            as a topological space. These two
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint"} adjoint
            operations turn out to exhibit the homotopy theory of simplicial sets as being equivalent (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+equivalence"}> Quillen equivalent
            ) to the homotopy theory of topological spaces. For some purposes, working in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+homotopy+theory"} simplicial homotopy theory
            is preferable over working with topological homotopy theory.
          #TopologicalSimplex.num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              For
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              %strong
                %a{:href => "simplex#TopologicalSimplex"} topological n-simplex
              is, up to
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homeomorphism"} homeomorphism
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              whose underlying set is the subset
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi n
                    %mo ≔
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mover
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} →
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %munderover
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                      %mi n
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi i
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi and
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ∀
                    %mi i
                    %mo .
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi i
                    %mo ≥
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo ⊂
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\Delta^n \coloneqq
                    \\{
                    \\vec x \in \mathbb{R}^{n+1}
                    |
                    \\sum_{i = 0 }^n x_i = 1 \; and \;
                    \\forall i . x_i \geq 0
                    \\}
                    \\subset \mathbb{R}^{n+1}
            %p
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo +
                          %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{n+1}
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subspace+topology"} subspace topology
              induces from the canonical topology in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo +
                          %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{n+1}
          .num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 0
              this is the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/point"} point
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mn 0
                      %mo =
                      %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^0 = *
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 1
              this is the standard
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interval+object"} interval object
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Δ
                        %mn 1
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^1 = [0,1]
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 2
              this is the filled triangle.
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 3
              this is the filled tetrahedron.
          #FaceInclusionInBarycentricCoords.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              For
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} n
                    %mo ≥
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \n \geq 1
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi k
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \leq k \leq n
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                th
                = succeed "-face" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-1)
              of the topological
              = succeed "-simplex," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalSimplex"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi δ
                      %mi k
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ↪
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\delta_k : \Delta^{n-1} \hookrightarrow \Delta^n
            %p
              induced under the coordinate presentation of def.
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalSimplex"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                    %mo ↪
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{R}^n \hookrightarrow \mathbb{R}^{n+1}
            %p
              which “omits” the
              = succeed "th" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↦
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi k
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (x_0, \cdots , x_{n-1}) \mapsto (x_0, \cdots, x_{k-1} , 0 , x_{k}, \cdots, x_n)
                    \\,.
          .num_example
            %h6#example_2 Example
            %p The inclusion
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi δ
                      %mn 0
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\delta_0 : \Delta^0 \to \Delta^1
            %p is the inclusion
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo ↪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\{1\} \hookrightarrow [0,1]
            %p of the “right” end of the standard interval. The other inclusion
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi δ
                      %mn 1
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\delta_1 : \Delta^0 \to \Delta^1
            %p
              is that of the “left” end
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mo ↪
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{0\} \hookrightarrow [0,1]
          %p
            %img{:src => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/faceanddegeneracymaps.jpg", :width => "500"}/
          %p
            (graphics taken from
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/simplicial+set#Friedman08"} Friedman 08
          #DegeneracyProjectionsInBarycentricCoords.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi k
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \leq k \lt n
              the
              %strong
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                th degenerate
                = succeed "-simplex" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n)
              is the surjective map
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi σ
                      %mi k
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\sigma_k : \Delta^{n} \to \Delta^{n-1}
            %p
              induced under the barycentric coordinates of def.
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalSimplex"}
              under the surjection
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbb{R}^{n+1} \to \mathbb{R}^n
            %p which sends
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↦
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi k
                    %mo +
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (x_0, \cdots, x_n) \mapsto (x_0, \cdots, x_{k} + x_{k+1}, \cdots, x_n)
                    \\,.
          #SingularSimplex.num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ∈
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi ℕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              %strong
                singular
                = succeed "-simplex" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+map"} continuous map
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi σ
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\sigma : \Delta^n \to X
            %p
              from the topological
              = succeed "-simplex," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              = succeed "," do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalSimplex"}
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %p Write
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Sing
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi n
                    %mo ≔
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi Top
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (Sing X)_n \coloneqq Hom_{Top}(\Delta^n , X)
            %p
              for the set of singular
              = succeed "-simplices" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            %img{:src => "http://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/singularsimplices.jpg", :width => "500"}/
          %p
            (graphics taken from
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/simplicial+set#Friedman08"} Friedman 08
          %p
            The sets
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Sing
                  %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Sing X)_\bullet
            here are closely related by an interlocking system of maps that make them form what is called a
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+simplicial+complex"} singular simplicial complex
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            = succeed "." do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SingularSimplicialComplex"}
          %p
            Since the topological
            = succeed "-simplices" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta^n
            from def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#TopologicalSimplex"}
            sit inside each other by the face inclusions of def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#FaceInclusionInBarycentricCoords"}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi δ
                    %mi k
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\delta_k : \Delta^{n-1} \to \Delta^{n}
          %p
            and project onto each other by the degeneracy maps, def.
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#DegeneracyProjectionsInBarycentricCoords"}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi σ
                    %mi k
                  %mo :
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi Δ
                    %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\sigma_k : \Delta^{n+1} \to \Delta^n
          %p we dually have functions
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi d
                    %mi k
                  %mo ≔
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mi Top
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi δ
                    %mi k
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Sing
                  %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi n
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Sing
                  %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  d_k \coloneqq Hom_{Top}(\delta_k, X) : (Sing X)_n \to (Sing X)_{n-1}
          %p
            that send each singular
            = succeed "-simplex" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "-face" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi s
                    %mi k
                  %mo ≔
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mi Top
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi σ
                    %mi k
                  %mo ,
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Sing
                  %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi n
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Sing
                  %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  s_k \coloneqq Hom_{Top}(\sigma_k,X) : (Sing X)_{n} \to (Sing X)_{n+1}
          %p
            that regard an
            = succeed "-simplex" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "-simplex." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo +
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n+1)
          #SimplicialSet.num_defn
            %h6#definition_5 Definition
            %p
              A
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+set"} simplicial set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi sSet
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S \in sSet
              is
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  for each
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi S
                          %mi n
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi Set
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S_n \in Set
                  – the
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %strong
                      set of
                      = succeed "-" do
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %mi n
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplices"} simplices
              %li
                %p
                  for each
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+map"} injective map
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi δ
                          %mi i
                        %mo :
                        %mover
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ¯
                        %mo →
                        %mover
                          %mi n
                          %mo ¯
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \delta_i : \overline{n-1} \to \overline{n}
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/totally+ordered+sets"} totally ordered sets
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                        %mo ≔
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %mn 0
                        %mo &lt;
                        %mn 1
                        %mo &lt;
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mo &lt;
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar n \coloneqq \{ 0 \lt 1 \lt \cdots \lt n \}
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi d
                          %mi i
                        %mo :
                        %msub
                          %mi S
                          %mi n
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi S
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_i : S_{n} \to S_{n-1}
                  – the
                  = succeed "th" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
                  %strong face map
                  on
                  = succeed "-simplices;" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %li
                %p
                  for each
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surjective+map"} surjective map
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi σ
                          %mi i
                        %mo :
                        %mover
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo +
                            %mn 1
                          %mo ¯
                        %mo →
                        %mover
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma_i : \overline{n+1} \to \bar n
                  of
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/totally+ordered+sets"} totally ordered sets
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi σ
                          %mi i
                        %mo :
                        %msub
                          %mi S
                          %mi n
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi S
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo +
                            %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sigma_i : S_{n} \to S_{n+1}
                  – the
                  = succeed "th" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
                  %strong degeneracy map
                  on
                  = succeed "-simplices;" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %p
              such that these functions satisfy the
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+identities"} simplicial identities
          #SimplicialIdentities.num_defn
            %h6#definition_6 Definition
            %p
              The
              %strong simplicial identities
              satisfied by face and degeneracy maps as above are (whenever these maps are composable as indicated):
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi d
                          %mi i
                        %mo ∘
                        %msub
                          %mi d
                          %mi j
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi d
                          %mrow
                            %mi j
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo ∘
                        %msub
                          %mi d
                          %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_i \circ d_j  = d_{j-1} \circ d_i
                  if
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo &lt;
                          %mi j
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \lt j
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi s
                          %mi i
                        %mo ∘
                        %msub
                          %mi s
                          %mi j
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %mi s
                          %mi j
                        %mo ∘
                        %msub
                          %mi s
                          %mrow
                            %mi i
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s_i \circ s_j  = s_j \circ s_{i-1}
                  if
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi i
                          %mo &gt;
                          %mi j
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \gt j
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi d
                          %mi i
                        %mo ∘
                        %msub
                          %mi s
                          %mi j
                        %mo =
                        %mrow
                          %mo {
                          %mrow
                            %mtable
                              %mtr
                                %mtd
                                  %msub
                                    %mi s
                                    %mrow
                                      %mi j
                                      %mo −
                                      %mn 1
                                  %mo ∘
                                  %msub
                                    %mi d
                                    %mi i
                                %mtd
                                  %mi if
                                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                  %mi i
                                  %mo &lt;
                                  %mi j
                              %mtr
                                %mtd
                                  %mi id
                                %mtd
                                  %mi if
                                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                  %mi i
                                  %mo =
                                  %mi j
                                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                  %mi or
                                  %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                                  %mi i
                                  %mo =
                                  %mi j
                                  %mo +
                                  %mn 1
                              %mtr
                                %mtd
                                  %msub
                                    %mi s
                                    %mi j
                                  %mo ∘
                                  %msub
                                    %mi d
                                    %mrow
                                      %mi i
                                      %mo −
                                      %mn 1
                                %mtd
                                  %mi if
                                  %mi i
                                  %mo &gt;
                                  %mi j
                                  %mo +
                                  %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_i \circ s_j =  \left\{ \array{ s_{j-1} \circ d_i &amp;  if \;  i \lt j \\ id &amp; if  \;  i = j \; or \; i = j+1 \\ s_j \circ d_{i-1} &amp;  if i \gt j+1 } \right.
          %p
            It is straightforward to check by explicit inspection that the evident injection and restriction maps between the sets of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singular+simplices"} singular simplices
            make
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi Sing
                  %mi X
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (Sing X)_\bullet
            into a simplicial set. However for working with this, it is good to streamline a little:
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_7 Definition
            %p
              The
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex+category"} simplex category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Δ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Delta
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
              on the free categories of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≔
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                            %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≔
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                            %mn 0
                            %mo →
                            %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≔
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                            %mn 0
                            %mo →
                            %mn 1
                            %mo →
                            %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi ⋮
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    [0] &amp; \coloneqq \{0\}
                    \\\
                    [1] &amp; \coloneqq \{0 \to 1\}
                    \\\
                    [2] &amp; \coloneqq \{0 \to 1 \to 2\}
                    \\\
                    \\vdots
                    \\end{aligned}
                    \\,.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              This is called the “simplex category” because we are to think of the object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [n]
              as being the “
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spine"}> spine
              ” of the
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex"} simplex
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 2
              we think of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \to 1 \to 2
              as the “spine” of the triangle. This becomes clear if we don’t just draw the morphisms that
              %em generate
              the category
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [n]
